  STEP #03
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_problem_07_step_03
  step_number: 3
  instruction_preview: Inspect the hot and cold inlet hoses along their full visible length. Make sure neither hose is sharply bent, crushed, twisted, or trapped against the washer.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_parent_008_child_008']
  page_numbers: [7, 8]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems

  STEP #04
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_problem_07_step_04
  step_number: 4
  instruction_preview: Check both hose connections at the washer and at the water supply. Each connection should be seated correctly and should not show leakage.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_parent_008_child_008']
  page_numbers: [7, 8]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems

  STEP #05
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_problem_07_step_05
  step_number: 5
  instruction_preview: If the problem involves slow or no filling, inspect the inlet screens at the hose connections for visible dirt or sediment. Clean only the accessible screens using the procedure recommended by the manual; do not damage or remove internal components.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_parent_008_child_008']
  page_numbers: [7, 8]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems

  STEP #06
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_problem_07_step_06
  step_number: 6
  instruction_preview: Reconnect the hoses securely, restore the water supply, and run a short test cycle. Observe whether water enters normally.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_parent_008_child_008']
  page_numbers: [7, 8]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems

  STEP #07
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_problem_07_step_07
  step_number: 7
  instruction_preview: If the washer still has a fill problem after the external checks, the cause may involve the water valve, pressure sensing system, wiring, or control board. These are service-level checks and should not be opened or tested as a DIY repair.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_12_Maintenance_Problems_parent_008_child_008']
  page_numbers: [7, 8]
