problem_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01
problem_name: Washer does not turn on
document_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed
chunk_count: 1
max_rerank_score: 0.269603

  STEP #01
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_01
  step_number: 1
  instruction_preview: Make sure the washer is not currently in a power interruption. Check whether lights or another appliance on the same electrical circuit are working.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #02
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_02
  step_number: 2
  instruction_preview: Go to the washer's power cord and confirm that the plug is fully inserted into the electrical outlet. Do not rely only on looking at the plug; make sure it has not become partially disconnected.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #03
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_03
  step_number: 3
  instruction_preview: Inspect the plug and the visible portion of the power cord without touching exposed conductors. Look for cuts, melted areas, discoloration, loose parts, or signs of overheating.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #04
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_04
  step_number: 4
  instruction_preview: If the cord and plug appear normal, press the Power button once. Wait a few seconds and observe the control panel for any lights or display activity.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #05
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_05
  step_number: 5
  instruction_preview: If there is still no response, check the electrical outlet using a safe method. If you are not comfortable testing an outlet, have a qualified person verify that the outlet is supplying power.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #06
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_06
  step_number: 6
  instruction_preview: If the outlet has no power, do not attempt to repair the household wiring yourself. Restore the household electrical supply or contact a qualified electrician.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #07
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_07
  step_number: 7
  instruction_preview: If the outlet has power, disconnect the washer from the outlet before doing any further external inspection. Wait briefly, reconnect it securely, and press Power again.
  chunk_ids: ['WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_parent_002_child_002']
  page_numbers: [2, 3]
  source_document: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed

  STEP #08
  --------
  step_id: WA5471ABP_01_Starting_Power_Problems_Detailed_problem_01_step_08
  step_number: 8
  instruction_preview: If the washer remains completely unresponsive even though the outlet has power, stop the procedure. The problem may be inside the washer's power/control system and should be diagnosed by service personnel. After completing the steps Do not remove the washer's electrical covers or attempt to test live internal components as a DIY repair. Safety: Do not bypass a fuse, circuit breaker, grounding connection, or other protective device.
